diwall (1.21.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Documentation completeness pass across docs/: docs/GUIDE.md Case 4
    corrected (falsely described Basic Auth as an open gap after it had
    shipped), docs/RETOUR_EXPERIENCE.md FR-86 marked resolved,
    docs/MANUEL.md/FAQ_LLM.md/README.md extended with --http-credentials
    (previously undocumented in the operational manual, FAQ, and
    capabilities table). Two real leaks found and fixed along the way: a
    live service hostname in docs/RETOUR_EXPERIENCE.md and shot.py's own
    comments (not in the preflight pattern list — a gap to close
    separately), and a stale --guide-version token (3.8) in three
    still-live usage examples.

  * --http-credentials (shot.py, rpa.py): resolves HTTP Basic Auth
    (RFC 7617) credentials from the vault and injects them at
    browser-context creation, scoped to the target's origin
    ("send": "unauthorized") — never sent to a third-party origin loaded
    in the same context. Fallback documented for proxies that never issue
    a clean 401: "send": "always", still origin-scoped, never a hand-built
    Authorization header (not yet exercised against a real target).
  * Vault keys: http_username/http_password tried first, falls back to
    plain username/password if absent — found and fixed during real-target
    validation against a live Caddy-protected admin interface, which
    confirmed send: "unauthorized" resolves a real challenge on the first
    attempt (the actual gap was key naming, not the send mode).
  * boussole.http_credentials_actif is conditioned on the flag being
    active AND the initial navigation not ending in 401 — never just the
    CLI flag, same discipline as the stealth_actif fix (v1.16.0/FR-79).
    boussole.http_auth_requise flags an unresolved 401 distinctly from
    the WAF signal.
  * scenarios/schema.json: optional root property http_credentials,
    combinable with the CLI flag (OR), same pattern as shadow_dom.
  * Non-presumption rule (CLAUDE.md Règle n°7, docs/GUIDE_LLM.md):
    never affirm a Diwall capability is absent, never presume one exists,
    without checking the action tables first.
  * docs/GUIDE_LLM.md compressed to the 250-line budget promised in
    CLAUDE.md (was 413 lines) — scripts/verifier-coherence.sh now fails
    on any future regression of this budget.
  * docs/GUIDE.md: four new anonymized demonstration cases (self-hosted
    observability/analytics dashboard, ticketing platform administration,
    local events tracking, e-commerce access under Citizen Navigation) —
    tools, brands and the operator generalised by functional category,
    never named — kept reusable as prompt templates regardless of which
    specific product a reader is running.
  * scenarios/interoperabilite/: local Basic Auth fixture (real 401
    challenge, no third-party dependency) added as a permanent regression
    fixture. scenarios/v1.21.0_validation/: 3/3 tests green.
  * Resynchronised scenarios/v1.18.0_validation/'s hardcoded guide-version
    token (3.7 -> 3.9) — pre-existing staleness found while running the
    regression suite, not a functional regression.

 -- Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>  Tue, 14 Jul 2026 11:31:27 +0200

diwall (1.20.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * journal.py --erreurs: store_true flag filtering resultat != "succes",
    same pattern as the existing --mutatif filter.
  * latences_actions: shot.py::executer_actions() now measures per-action
    wall-clock time (time.time() around each dispatch), exposed as an
    always-present JSON root key ({"index", "type", "latence_ms"} per
    entry). Complements the existing global citoyennete.duree_totale_ms.
  * Guide-read lock re-armed: notice-version 3.7 -> 3.8 (lib/preflight_guide.py
    resynchronised in the same commit) — GUIDE_LLM_MONITORING.md routing row
    updated for both new items (notice-version 1.9 -> 1.10).
  * Documentation: docs/MANUEL.md and docs/GUIDE_LLM_MONITORING.md document
    latences_actions and journal.py --erreurs.
  * scenarios/v1.20.0_validation/: 3/3 tests green (journal.py --erreurs
    filter, latences_actions always-present + structure end-to-end).

